{"name":"Laundry Blue","hex":"#a2adb3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"laundry blue","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A bluing ."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/laundry_blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bluing (fabric)","blocks":[{"text":"Bluing, laundry blue, dolly blue or washing blue is a household product used to improve the appearance of textiles, especially white fabrics. Used during laundering, it adds a trace of blue dye to the fabric."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bluing_(fabric)","wikidata":"Q2596268"},{"title":"Laundry","blocks":[{"text":"Laundry is the washing of clothing and other textiles, and, more broadly, their drying and ironing as well. Laundry has been part of history since humans began to wear clothes, so the methods by which different cultures have dealt with this universal human need are of interest to several branches of scholarship."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Italian_hanging_laundry.jpg/330px-Italian_hanging_laundry.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laundry","wikidata":"Q852100"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/M0354_1951-77-038_2.jpg/500px-M0354_1951-77-038_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/M0354_1951-77-038_2.jpg/500px-M0354_1951-77-038_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Laundry bluing kit from France, with the bluing pellets.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AM0354_1951-77-038_2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Laundry_1806.PNG/500px-Laundry_1806.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Laundry_1806.PNG/500px-Laundry_1806.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"\"Man and woman washing linen in a brook\", from William Henry Pyne's Microcosm (1806). Unusually, this is depicted as a mixed-sex activity.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALaundry_1806.PNG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Laundry_is_being_done_by_a_woman_in_the_river_near_Kiou_Ka_Cham_Laos_26Nov2005.jpg/500px-Laundry_is_being_done_by_a_woman_in_the_river_near_Kiou_Ka_Cham_Laos_26Nov2005.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Laundry_is_being_done_by_a_woman_in_the_river_near_Kiou_Ka_Cham_Laos_26Nov2005.jpg/1280px-Laundry_is_being_done_by_a_woman_in_the_river_near_Kiou_Ka_Cham_Laos_26Nov2005.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Laundry_is_being_done_by_a_woman_in_the_river_near_Kiou_Ka_Cham_Laos_26Nov2005.jpg/500px-Laundry_is_bein